      "body": "I think that, no matter how the code is restructured, the outcome should be that we have a unit test with the kind of scenario from the original report (`/b_allocRead` with synchronous completion message (`/b_query`) and subsequent `/sync`) that ensures it matches scsynth's order (which I would say constitutes the \"spec\"). For client systems using SuperCollider, it's crucial that the order of message arrival is not subject to any interpretation, and that both server implementations absolutely match here. 2c",
